Subject: conf/settings.xml: on OpenVMS, the javadoc tool and tar's user ids

Two plugins fail on OpenVMS with their defaults (NOTES N20):

- maven-javadoc-plugin looks for ${java.home}/../bin/javadoc and, not
  finding it (the file is JAVADOC.EXE), stops with "Unable to find javadoc
  command". Its javadocExecutable property names the image.
- maven-assembly-plugin's tar archives (plexus-archiver) failed with
  "user id '8388673' is too big ( > 2097151 )": the file owner's UIC
  ([group,member] as one number) does not fit the old tar header. With
  assembly.tarLongFileMode=posix, plexus-archiver writes big ids, and long
  names, in pax headers, which every current tar reads.

Both are properties in the openvms profile, so a project's own
configuration still wins. Nothing changes on other systems.

VMS-only, not for upstream.

--- a/conf/settings.xml	2026-11-11 07:25:08.350317114 +0000
+++ b/conf/settings.xml	2026-11-11 07:25:08.368642632 +0000
@@ -268,6 +268,12 @@
       </activation>
       <properties>
         <argLine>-Xms8m -Xmx64m -XX:+UseSerialGC -XX:ReservedCodeCacheSize=16m</argLine>
+        <!-- The javadoc tool: the plugin looks for bin/javadoc, which is
+             JAVADOC.EXE here (vms-maven, NOTES N20). -->
+        <javadocExecutable>${java.home}/../bin/javadoc.exe</javadocExecutable>
+        <!-- tar archives: an OpenVMS UIC as a tar user id is too big for the
+             old format; posix writes it, and long names, in pax headers. -->
+        <assembly.tarLongFileMode>posix</assembly.tarLongFileMode>
       </properties>
     </profile>
   </profiles>
